/// Behavioral API documentation for the Roadie Roster backend.
/// Static Markdown authored from the current backend source; reads no state.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Roadie Roster Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nBackend for **Roadie Roster**, the new-hire tracking app for Bubba's 33 store #975 in Lake Charles, LA (opening Mon Feb 8, 2027). It stores store configuration, positions (stations) with build-to targets, the opening schedule, checklists, retention settings, roadie cards, kiosk sign-up submissions, access grants, the admin-set kiosk PIN, the phase-2/3 records (orientation check-off, attendance, training groups, trainer notes, leader talks, final sign-offs, alerts), the Opening Questions section, and crew events (pre-opening get-togethers with per-roadie answers and attendance).\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery method that reads or writes application data requires a **signed (non-anonymous) caller**. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nSigning in is not enough: a principal must be **registered** before any role-guarded call succeeds. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend and calls `requestAccess()` once. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\nA **direct API caller** (an agent that never loads the frontend) must first call `_initialize_access_control()` once as a signed-in caller. The platform's shared authorization assigns the role by whether the caller is the first initializer:\n\n- The **first** initializer of `_initialize_access_control()` becomes `#admin` in the shared authorization state (the shared authorization owner).\n- Every **later** initializer receives the default role, which grants no application access until an Admin approves them.\n\nAfter that, call `requestAccess()` to create a pending request, and an Admin must call `approveUser(...)` before role-guarded methods work. An unregistered or anonymous caller on a guarded endpoint traps with a message such as `Not registered` or `Unauthorized`; the exact text comes from the shared authorization package and from `Auth.requireRegistered`.\n\n### Roles\n\nRoles are `#admin`, `#managingPartner`, `#storeManager`, `#trainingManager`, `#trainer`, `#visitingManager`, `#leadership`, `#kiosk`, `#integration`. The Managing Partner has full Admin rights. `#kiosk` and `#integration` are restricted: the kiosk may only submit sign-ups and check the PIN, and the integration role may read **only** the Shareable export — it is refused on shift boards, Today, the Dashboard and every other read. Only a Managing Partner may grant the Managing Partner role, or change, expire or remove a Managing Partner's grant; an Admin may do so only when no non-expired Managing Partner exists. The last active admin can never be demoted, end-dated or removed.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Timestamps** are `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (signed). Convert with `Time.now()` semantics; negative values are valid pre-1970 instants.\n- **Identifiers** (`RoadieId`, `PositionId`, `CrewId`, `ChangeLogId`, `QuestionId`, `SuggestionId`, `EventId`, `SignupId`) are `Nat`.\n- **Principals** identify users; `?Principal` means optional (for example a crew with no leader).\n- **Optional values** (`?T`) are Candid `opt`; `null` means absent. Blobs (`PhotoRef`, `SignatureRef`) are object-storage references, not raw bytes.\n- **Dates** that are date-only are stored as UTC day starts; schedule times use the store time zone (America/Chicago).\n- **Demo mode**: while demo mode is on, every query and export returns only demo records and every write targets demo data; demo records are invisible when demo mode is off. Demo mode auto-turns off after 8 hours. A signed-in caller with no stored demo role gets **no** demo role at all (there is no default to demo Admin), so demo mode never grants access to someone who was never approved. Opening Questions, its history and scoreboard, its alerts and the store settings always use the caller's **real** role, never a demo role, so demo mode can never raise anyone's access to real data. While demo mode is on, a signed-in caller with no real grant may still read the non-sensitive store details the demo screens need (store name, opening date, positions) through `getStoreDemoView()`; every other store setting stays on the real role.\n\n## Store and configuration\n\n- `getStoreInfo()` / `updateStoreInfo(info)` — read or update store name, location, opening date, logos and settings. `getStoreInfo` uses the caller's real role (any real, non-expired role except Kiosk and Integration); writes are Admin/Store Manager only.- `getStoreDemoView()` — the non-sensitive store details a demo viewer needs while demo mode is on: `{ appName; storeNumber; locationName; openingDate; timeZone; positions }`. Available to any signed-in caller while demo mode is on and refused when it is off; it never exposes the other store settings.\\n- `getStoreLogo()` — public query returning the main and secondary logo references for the kiosk and sign-in screens.\\n- `listPositions()`, `createPosition`, `updatePosition`, `deletePosition`, `adjustBuildTo(positionId, opening, afterOpening)` — position CRUD and build-to targets (Admin/Store Manager).\\n- `listSchedule`, `createScheduleEvent`, `updateScheduleEvent`, `deleteScheduleEvent` — the opening schedule events.\\n- `getChecklists` / `updateChecklists` — paperwork and other checklist items, including `enabled` and `shortLabel`.\\n- `getRetentionSettings` / `updateRetentionSettings` — data retention policy.\\n- `saveStoreTemplate`, `downloadStoreTemplate`, `loadStoreTemplate` — export/import a store template (positions, schedule, checklists) with no people data.\\n- `getUniformSettings` / `updateUniformSettings`, `getUniformOrder` — uniform defaults, size curve, buffer and the derived order; the uniform viewer is Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager or Training Manager.\\n\\n## Roadies\\n\\n- `listRoadies()`, `getRoadie(id)`, `getPhoto(id)`, `listRosterForPosition(positionId)` — read roadie cards and photos.\\n- `updateRoadieDetails(id, profile)`, `changePosition(...)` — edit a roadie (Admin/Store Manager).\\n- `archiveRoadie(id, reason)` / `rehireRoadie(id, reason)` — archive requires a reason, rehire requires a non-blank reason (a blank one traps \"A rehire reason is required\"); rehire returns the roadie to pending, assigns the next upcoming orientation session when one exists (otherwise keeps the roadie's existing orientation session) and clears any final sign-off they had.\\n- `getContactSet(id)` / `updateContactSet(id, contactSet)` — contact information, visible only to Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager, Kitchen Manager and Service Manager.\\n- `getRosterSummary()` — per-position on-hand and build-to counts.\\n- `resignAvailability(id, signature)` — record a signed availability resignation.\\n- `isMinor(id)` — whether a roadie is under 18 in store time.\\n- `listChangeLog()` — the change log; every write is recorded.\\n\\n## Crews\\n\\n- `listCrews()`, `listCrewSummaries()` — crews with leader and member counts.\\n- `createCrew(name, leaderPrincipal)`, `updateCrew(id, name, leaderPrincipal)`, `deleteCrew(id)` — Admin/Store Manager only; a crew owner may be an Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager or Training Manager; a manager may own only one crew, and delete is blocked while the crew has members.\\n\\n## Sign-ups (kiosk)\\n\\n- `submitSignup(...)` — kiosk sign-up submission; requires Kiosk, Store Manager, Admin or Managing Partner and caps text field lengths.\\n- `listPendingSignups()`, `getSignup(id)`, `getSignupPhoto(id)`, `findDuplicates(...)` — review pending sign-ups; the approvals queue and approve/reject are open to Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager, Kitchen Manager and Service Manager.\\n- `approveSignup(...)` / `rejectSignup(...)` — approve (creating a roadie) or reject a sign-up.\\n\\n## Access and users\\n\\n- `requestAccess()`, `getMyAccess()`, `getMyPendingRequest()` — the caller's own access state. `requestAccess()` refuses the anonymous (signed-out) identity with a trap.\\n- `submitStaffProfile(profile)`, `updateMyStaffProfile(profile)` — the caller's own profile. Both refuse the reserved work email `DEMO` with a trap; demo leaders are recognised by their system-actor approver, never by a work email, so a user who types `DEMO` is still an ordinary user.\\n- `bootstrapAdmin()` — only when no admin exists.\\n- `listPendingUsers()`, `listAccessGrants()`, `listLeaders()` — Admin views.\\n- `approveUser(...)`, `updateUserRole(...)`, `updateTrainerStations(...)`, `updateAccessEnd(...)`, `removeUser(...)` — Admin user management; the last admin cannot be demoted, overwritten or end-dated.\\n- `adminCount()`, `accessEndForDay(...)` — helpers for admin count and access end dates (11:59:59 PM America/Chicago).\\n\\n## Orientation and training (phase 2/3)\\n\\n- `getDashboard()`, `getToday()` — dashboard and Today data. Both refuse the Integration role with a trap.\\n- `getOrientationCheckoff`, `recordAttendance`, `listAttendanceForEvent`, `getOrientationSessionView`, `markPresent`, `undoPresent`, `moveRoadieToSession`, `moveAllRoadiesToSession`, `archiveNoShows`, `listOrientationSessions`, `listUnassignedPendingRoadies` — orientation sessions and attendance.\\n- `getUniformCheckoff` / `saveUniformCheckoff` — uniform check-off.\\n- `setPaperworkItems(...)` — record paperwork item completion.\\n- `getShiftBoard`, `listShiftBoards`, `saveShiftBoard`, `copyShiftBoard`, `autoFillShiftBoard`, `clearShiftBoard` — training shift boards, editable by Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager, Training Manager, Kitchen Manager and Service Manager; a roadie may appear in at most one group or in Off per shift. Reading a shift board (`getShiftBoard`, `listShiftBoards`) refuses the Integration role with a trap.\\n- `listGroupChangeNotices`, `dismissGroupChangeNotice`, `getMyGroup`, `getMyCrew` — trainer/manager views.\\n- `addTrainerNote`, `updateTrainerNote`, `listTrainerNotes` — trainer notes. `addTrainerNote(note)` may be called by Trainer, Training Manager, Kitchen Manager, Service Manager, Store Manager, Managing Partner or Admin; a Trainer may add only for a roadie in their own stations, everyone else for any roadie. It refuses a note whose Did well and Work on are both blank, a field over 1,000 characters, an archived roadie, and a roadie from the other demo partition (\"Roadie not found\"). `updateTrainerNote(note)` is author-only and locked 24 hours after creation; it also refuses a blank note and a field over 1,000 characters. `listTrainerNotes(roadieId)` returns notes newest first, each carrying the author's display name in `authorName`; who may read is unchanged (Integration sees nothing, a Trainer only roadies in their stations).\\n- `createLeaderTalk(talk)`, `setLeaderTalkAttendance(id, attendees)`, `deleteLeaderTalk(id)` — leader talks. Creating a talk, changing its group and deleting a talk are allowed for Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager and Training Manager only. A group is refused when larger than the store's `leaderTalkSize`, when it holds an archived roadie, a roadie from the other demo partition, or the same roadie twice. A blank talk name defaults to the store's `leaderTalkName` plus \" · Group N\". A talk created while demo mode is on is a demo talk; a write to the other partition is rejected. Every create, attendance change and delete is recorded in the change log.\n- `listLeaderTalks()` — every leader talk in the current demo partition, sorted by day then id, each with its id, name, day, `isDemo` and its attendees' `roadieId` and `displayName`. Readable by Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager, Training Manager, Kitchen Manager, Service Manager, Leadership and Visiting Manager; refused for Trainer, Kiosk and Integration.\n- `recordFinalSignOff(signOff)` — the roadie's training sign-off, separate from Opening Questions Final. Trainer (only roadies in their own stations), Training Manager, Kitchen Manager, Service Manager, Store Manager, Managing Partner and Admin may record. Only an active, non-archived roadie can be signed off; any other roadie is refused, and a roadie from the other demo partition traps `Roadie not found`. `outcome` is `#certified` or `#needsMoreTime(reason)`, where the reason must be non-blank and at most 1,000 characters. Certified sets the roadie's status to `#certified`; Needs more time sets it to `#needsMoreTime`. A later sign-off replaces the earlier one and each is written to the change log. A sign-off recorded while demo mode is on is a demo sign-off.\n- `clearFinalSignOff(roadieId)` — Admin, Managing Partner and Store Manager only: removes the sign-off, puts the roadie's status back to `#active`, and logs it; refused while the sign-off belongs to the other demo partition.\n- `getFinalSignOff(roadieId)` — the sign-off with the signer's display name in `signedByName`, or null. Readable by every role that can read that roadie (not Kiosk or Integration; a Trainer only for their stations).\\n- `listAlerts`, `acknowledgeAlert` — alerts.\\n- `recordCheckIn`, `getCheckInBoard`, `listAbsentAlerts`, `excuseAbsentAlert`, `archiveAbsentAlert`, `moveAbsentRoadieToOtherShift` — check-in and absence handling. Checking people in and changing check-ins is allowed for Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager, Training Manager, Kitchen Manager and Service Manager; the absent-alert actions (excuse, archive, move) stay Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager and Training Manager only.\\n\\n## Exports and gift bags\\n\\n- `buildShareableExport()` — the Shareable export (no contact information); the only read available to the integration role, and available to every other read role except Kiosk.\\n- `buildFullExport()` — the full export including the contact set; Admin, Managing Partner and Store Manager only (Kitchen Manager and Service Manager are refused).\\n- `getGiftBags(filter)` — the gift-bag shopping list and labels; Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager or Training Manager.\\n\\n## Opening Questions\\n\\nQuestions are grouped into sections and areas (Kitchen, Service, Both, Dan). Owners are computed live from the current, non-expired grants, never stored per question: the Kitchen Manager owns Kitchen and Both, the Service Manager owns Service and Both, and the Managing Partner owns Dan. A manager whose access has expired no longer counts as an owner anywhere (Ready for final, Needs my approval, the scoreboard, Next and nudges). **Every** Opening Questions call (list, read, history, scoreboard, comment, reply, suggest, approve, answer, export) requires the caller's real, non-expired role to be Admin, Managing Partner, Store Manager, Training Manager, Kitchen Manager or Service Manager; every other role traps with an access error, and the caller's real role is used, never a demo role. There is **no question status**: a question is counted as answered when its answer text is not blank. Approvals, Ready for final and Final are unchanged.\\n\\n- `listOpeningQuestions(tab, filter)` — questions for a tab (`#myQuestions`, `#needsMyApproval`, `#all`, `#decisionDue`, `#final`, `#readyForFinal`) with combined filters (section, area, search). `#myQuestions` lists every question the caller owns, approved or not, in imported order (section order, then question order) and is the default tab for owners. `#needsMyApproval` lists the questions the caller owns that they have not approved and that are not Final. `#readyForFinal` is visible to the Managing Partner only. Every `QuestionView` carries `myApproved` and `myApprovedAt` (the caller's own approval timestamp, or null) so the page can show a \\\"You approved\\\" chip on every tab. Each view carries only discussion counts (`commentCount` for top-level comments, `replyCount` for replies across the question's suggestions), never the full discussion, so the list stays small; load a question's discussion with `getOpeningQuestionDiscussion(id)` when its card is opened.- `getOpeningQuestionDiscussion(id)` — one question's discussion: its `suggestions` and `comments` (each comment carries an optional `suggestionId`; a null `suggestionId` is a top-level comment, a non-null one is a reply to that suggestion). Loaded on demand when a card is opened, not with the list. Same role guard as every other Opening Questions call.- `getMyPendingOpeningQuestionApprovals()` — the caller's own pending-approval count (questions they own, not approved, not Final) for the Needs my approval tab badge.\\n- `getOpeningQuestionManagerScoreboard()` — the Managers scoreboard: one row per current question owner (Kitchen Managers, Service Managers and the Managing Partner) with `principal`, `displayName`, `role`, `ownedCount` (questions they own right now), `approvedCount` (of those, how many they have approved) and `pendingCount` (of those, how many still need their approval, excluding Final questions). Rows are sorted by most `pendingCount` first, then by display name, then principal, so the order is stable between refreshes. Counts follow the live ownership rules and change immediately after an approval or unapproval. Readable only by the Managing Partner and Admins; every other role is refused with a trap.\\n- `markOpeningQuestionsFinal(ids)` — mark several questions Final at once. Managing Partner only; every other role, including an Admin who is not the Managing Partner, is refused with a trap. Each question that is still ready for final (not already Final and every current owner has approved) is marked Final with one History entry and one change-log entry, exactly as single Mark final. A question that is already Final, no longer has every owner’s approval, or does not exist is skipped. Returns `{ markedCount; skippedCount }`.\\n- `getOpeningQuestionHistory(id)` — one question's change history, newest first: answer edits (with old and new text), approvals, unapprovals, Mark final, Reopen, and accepted or declined suggestions, each with the person and timestamp. Readable only by the Managing Partner and Admins; every other role is refused.\\n- `getOpeningQuestionsProgress()` — totals: `total`, `final` (questions the Managing Partner marked Final; answer text and owner approvals never count), `readyForFinal` (every owner approved but not Final yet), `answered` (non-blank answer text, kept for compatibility and not a Final count), `openSuggestions`, and per-section progress where each section reports its own `final` and `total`.\\n- `saveOpeningQuestionAnswer(id, answer)` — save an answer; changing the text clears its approvals. Refused while the question is Final (the Managing Partner must reopen it first).\\n- `approveOpeningQuestion(id)` / `withdrawOpeningQuestionApproval(id)` — the caller's own approval only; a caller can never add or remove another person's approval. Both are refused while the question is Final (the Managing Partner must reopen it first). Withdrawing is logged in the change log, returns the question to the caller's Needs my approval tab and drops it out of Ready for final.\\n- `markOpeningQuestionFinal(id)` / `reopenOpeningQuestion(id)` — Managing Partner only; marking Final raises the Final totals and the section's Final count, and reopen clears the final mark (lowering both again) while keeping the answer and discussion.\\n- `postOpeningQuestionSuggestion(id, proposedAnswer, note)`, `replyToOpeningQuestionSuggestion(id, suggestionId, text)`, `postOpeningQuestionComment(id, text)`, `decideOpeningQuestionSuggestion(id, suggestionId, accept)` — discussion; suggestions open a 48-hour window that drives the countdown and nudges only, and only an Admin decides. Accepting a suggestion is refused while the question is Final (the Managing Partner must reopen it first); declining stays allowed. A reply is accepted only while its suggestion is still pending (`#open`); once a suggestion is accepted or declined, new replies are refused with a trap. Text length limits are enforced here and in the frontend: an answer is at most 4,000 characters; a comment, reply or suggestion is at most 2,000; a trainer note is at most 1,000. Longer text is refused with a clear message naming the limit.\\n- `importOpeningQuestions(file)` — Admin only, only when no questions exist. The file's `who` and `status` fields are optional legacy fields: a blank `who` and a missing `status` are accepted, and both are ignored. Each question's `category` must be one of `kitchen`, `service`, `both` or `dan` (case-insensitive); any other value is rejected with an `#err` preview naming the section and question number.\\n- `clearOpeningQuestions(confirm)` — Admin only; `confirm` must be `CLEAR`. Clearing all questions also clears their history entries and nudge records, so nothing is left pointing at a deleted question.\\n- `getOpeningQuestionAlerts()`, `getOpeningQuestionEmailSettings()`, `updateOpeningQuestionEmailSettings(settings)` — alerts and the daily 7 AM email setting.\\n- `getOpeningQuestionDailyEmailStatus()` — the Admin > Opening Questions daily-email status: `{ lastSentAt; lastRecipientCount }`, when the last daily email went out (nanoseconds, or null when never sent) and to how many people. Readable by every role that can read the section. Read-only query.\\n- `sendOpeningQuestionTestEmail()` — send the caller's own work email immediately, even when nothing is waiting, marked as a test. **Admin and Managing Partner only**; every other role is refused with a trap. Refused while demo mode is on. Refused when the caller has no work email on their staff profile. The send is logged in the change log (success or failure) without the email address; a failed send traps. Not idempotent: each call sends another email.\\n- **Daily email.** While the daily email setting is on, a timer fires every day at 7:00 AM in the store time zone (from store settings) and arms the next day's timer before each run (so a trapping send cannot stop it) and on every upgrade. Each real, non-expired Kitchen Manager, Service Manager, Managing Partner and Admin with a work email on their staff profile receives at most one email per store-local day, and only when at least one item is waiting on them: questions needing their approval, open suggestion discussions they are in, Ready for final (Managing Partner), suggestion decisions due (Admin and Managing Partner), and the Finish-by date with days left or overdue. The subject names the store and number (for example \"Store 975 Opening Questions: 12 need your approval\") and the body links to the full Opening Qs address https://tlcroadieroster.com/opening-questions. The store day and Finish-by date always use the real current time, never the demo pretend date, so demo mode cannot shift or repeat a real email. Demo leaders, expired people and anyone with no work email are skipped. Each send, skip and failure is logged in the change log without the email address; a failed send for one person does not stop the others. A late or repeated timer run the same store day sends nothing more to anyone already emailed that day.\\n- `getOpeningQuestionHistory(id)` — one question's change history, newest first. **Managing Partner and Admins only**; every other role is refused with a trap. Each entry carries the question id, the change kind (`answerEdited`, `approved`, `approvalWithdrawn`, `markedFinal`, `reopened`, `suggestionAccepted`, `suggestionDeclined`), the principal who made the change, the timestamp in nanoseconds, and for answer edits the old and new answer text (null for every other kind). Entries are recorded from now on; a question with no recorded changes returns an empty array. This is a read-only query.\\n- `getOpeningQuestionFinishBy()` — the Opening Questions Finish-by date as the page reads it: `{ finishBy; daysLeft; daysOverdue }`. `finishBy` is the stored store-local calendar date (UTC-midnight nanoseconds) or null when unset. `daysLeft` is the whole number of store-local calendar days from today to that date (0 on the date itself and when unset); `daysOverdue` is the whole number of days past it (0 before the date and when unset). Readable by every role that can read the section (any readable role except Integration). Read-only query.\\n- `setOpeningQuestionFinishBy(finishBy)` — set (`?<date>`) or clear (`null`) the Finish-by date. **Managing Partner and Admins only**; every other role is refused with a trap. Refused while demo mode is on, like the other real Opening Questions settings. Every save and clear is written to the change log. Not idempotent in the log: each call records an entry.\\n- `sendOpeningQuestionNudge(manager)` — send an in-app nudge to one manager who still has questions needing their approval. **Managing Partner and Admins only**; every other role is refused with a trap. Refused while demo mode is on. The target must be a current question owner (Kitchen Manager, Service Manager or Managing Partner) with at least one question still needing their approval, otherwise it traps. One nudge per manager per store-local day: a second nudge the same day traps \\\"That manager was already nudged today\\\". The nudge stores the sender, the manager, the store-local day and the manager's pending count at that moment, and is written to the change log naming the sender and the manager nudged. The manager sees it as an in-app alert on their Today page and in their Opening Qs badge.\\n- `getMyOpeningQuestionNudges()` — the caller's own nudge alerts, newest first, each `{ senderName; pendingCount; sentAt }` where `senderName` is the sender's display name, `pendingCount` is a **live** count of how many questions still need the caller's approval right now (not the count from the day the nudge was sent), and `sentAt` is the timestamp in nanoseconds. An alert disappears once the caller has no questions left waiting on them, so the list is empty when nothing is pending. Readable by every role that can read the section; a caller with no nudge returns an empty array. Read-only query.\\n\\nAll Opening Questions writes are refused while demo mode is on and are recorded in the change log.\\n\\n## Crew events\n\nCrew events are pre-opening get-togethers for the whole crew (for example a barbecue). No events are built in and none are seeded. Each event has an id, name, start date and time, place, an optional note, a cancelled flag and an `isDemo` flag. Each roadie's answer is stored as one invite per event and roadie: answer (`going`, `cantGo`, `noAnswer`, default `noAnswer`), reason (required when the answer is `cantGo`, at most 1,000 characters), follow-up note (at most 1,000 characters), attendance (`yes`, `no`, `notMarked`), who last updated it and when, and `isDemo`.\n\n- `listCrewEvents()` — every event in the active demo partition, upcoming first (soonest first) then past (most recent first), each with the going / can't go / no answer counts. A viewer who leads a crew sees counts for their own crew only; every other viewer (for example Admin or Managing Partner who leads no crew) sees counts across every active, non-archived roadie in any crew in the active demo partition. Readable by every signed-in role that can read the roster; Kiosk and Integration are refused. Read-only query.\n- `getEventCrew(eventId, crewId)` — one event's crew list: the event header plus one row per active, non-archived roadie in the selected crew, with each roadie's answer, reason, follow-up note, attendance and `followUpDue` (a can't-go answer whose follow-up note is still empty 48 hours after it was recorded). Admin, Managing Partner and Store Manager may pass any `crewId`; a crew leader sees their own crew (passing another crew's id returns null). Returns null when the caller owns no crew and may not pick one. Read-only query.\n- `createCrewEvent(name, start, place, note)` — create an event. **Managing Partner and Admin only**; every other role is refused with a trap. `name` and `place` must be non-blank. Returns the new event id. Not idempotent: each call creates another event.\n- `updateCrewEvent(eventId, name, start, place, note)` — edit an event, including moving its start date and time. **Managing Partner and Admin only.** Moving an event keeps every answer, reason, follow-up and attendance already recorded.\n- `setCrewEventCancelled(eventId, cancelled)` — cancel or un-cancel an event. **Managing Partner and Admin only.** A cancelled event takes no new answers or attendance but keeps every recorded answer. There is no delete.\n- `saveEventAnswer(eventId, roadieId, answer, reason, followUpNote)` — record one roadie's answer, reason and follow-up note. A crew leader may record for roadies in their own crew; Admin, Managing Partner and Store Manager for any roadie. Only active, non-archived roadies in the active partition. A cancelled event takes no new answers (traps). A `cantGo` answer requires a non-blank reason (traps otherwise); the reason and the follow-up note are each at most 1,000 characters.\n- `markEventAttendance(eventId, roadieId, attendance)` — mark one roadie's attendance (`yes`, `no`, `notMarked`). Same authorization as saving an answer. Allowed only once the event's start has passed (traps before then); a cancelled event takes no new attendance.\n- `listAtRiskRoadies()` — the at-risk roadies: those with 2 or more non-cancelled events where the roadie's answer is can't go OR their attendance is no (counted once per event, never twice), flagged \"Orientation no-show risk\", each with `roadieId`, `name`, photo and `atRiskEvents` (the count of such events). The same 2-or-more rule drives the My crew flag and the Dashboard row. Manager query for the Dashboard Needs attention row; refused for non-manager roles. Read-only query.\n- `listUpcomingEvents()` — the next 3 non-cancelled events for the Today \"Upcoming events\" card, each with the going / can't go / no answer counts under the same rule as `listCrewEvents` (own crew when the viewer leads one, otherwise every crewed roadie in the active partition). Read-only query.\n\nEvery crew-events write is recorded in the change log and follows the demo partition: a write while demo mode is on targets demo data, and a write to the other partition is refused.\n\n## Demo mode\\n\\n- `getDemoState()`, `setDemoMode(...)`, `setDemoRole(...)`, `setDemoTrainerAs(...)`, `setDemoManagerAs(...)`, `setPretendDate(...)`, `getDemoDataSummary()`, `loadDemoData()`, `clearDemoData()`, `scheduleAutoOff()` — demo-mode control (Admin only for on/off).\\n\\n## Kiosk\\n\\n- `setKioskPin(pin)` — Admin only.\\n- `checkKioskPin(pin)` / `hasKioskPin()` — public queries used by the kiosk screen.\\n\\n## Seeding\\n\\n- `ensureSeeded()` — Admin only; seeds default positions, schedule and checklists when empty.\\n\\n## Errors, limits and retry safety\\n\\n- Guarded methods trap (rather than returning an error variant) when the caller is unregistered, anonymous or lacks the required role; the trap message names the missing permission.\\n- Writes are not idempotent in general: repeating a create call creates another record. Retry a failed write only after confirming it did not take effect.\\n- Destructive calls (`deletePosition`, `deleteCrew`, `clearOpeningQuestions`, `clearDemoData`, `removeUser`, `archiveRoadie`) take effect immediately and cannot be undone except by re-creating the data.\\n- `clearOpeningQuestions` requires the literal `CLEAR` confirmation string.\\n- Polling: `getMyAccess()` is safe to poll while waiting for approval; `getToday()` and `getDashboard()` are safe to poll for live counts. Prefer queries over updates for polling.\\n";
  };
};
